From: Konrad Pietrzak <konrad@erlang.org>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:06:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] snmp: Bound integer parsing in the BER decoder

Bounding the varbind value types was only half the job. Every
dec_int_tag/1 call site was still unbounded, so the v3 header fields, the
USM security parameters and all PDU integer fields accepted an arbitrary
number of BER content octets and built a bignum from them.
msgAuthoritativeEngineBoots and msgAuthoritativeEngineTime are parsed
before the message is authenticated, so that input is reachable pre-auth.

Give every integer field the content octet limit its type implies, named
after the type rather than spelled as a literal: four octets for the
INTEGER (0..2147483647) and Integer32 fields, five for the unsigned 32-bit
types, nine for Counter64. Remove the unlimited dec_int_tag/1 and
dec_integer_notag/1 wrappers so no call site can silently omit a limit,
and with them the infinity clause of dec_integer_notag/2, which is
unreachable once every caller passes a limit.

Signal a violation with exit rather than throw. All callers wrap decoding
in (catch ...) and match {'EXIT', Reason}; a thrown term is returned bare
and matched neither clause, so an over-long integer produced a case_clause
in snmpa_mpd instead of a discarded packet and an snmpInASNParseErrs
increment. Fields that re-tag the failure keep the {Size, Limit} pair and
use a distinct _bytesize suffix, so a length violation cannot be confused
with the value rejections from chk_msg_id/1 and friends.

dec_Counter64/2 had a second, separate signalling bug: it reported an
over-long Counter64 as throw({exit, {bad_counter64_length, BadSize}}), a
term no caller can match on either count. It now exits with the same
{bad_integer, {Size, Limit}} reason as every other integer field.

The chk_msg_id/1, chk_msg_max_size/1 and chk_msg_sec_model/1 range checks
are kept alongside the new limits. An octet cap is not a range check: four
legal octets still encode a negative msgID, and one octet still encodes a
msgMaxSize below the RFC 3412 floor of 484.

Related: GHSA-8qw4-2chm-mvj2
Aux Id: OTP-20346

Part of the fix for CVE-2026-59696.

(cherry picked from commit 2cf26f2238c904f5e7a621b971442e2c7b77db1a)

[Backport to OTP 26: OTP 26 has no dec_Counter64/snmp_pdus_basic codec
and decodes Counter64 inline, so the dec_Counter64/2 change is replaced
by using ?UINT64_MAX_OCTETS for the inline Counter64 limit added by the
previous commit. All other hunks ported as-is.]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Peter Lemenkov <lemenkov@gmail.com>

